7. **Arbitrary Update**: Vulnerable! The contract handles DeleteApplication but doesn't handle UpdateApplication at all. In Algorand, if an application doesn't explicitly reject UpdateApplication transactions, they will be approved by default. This means anyone can update the application code arbitrarily.

8. **Arbitrary Delete**: Not vulnerable. The contract properly handles DeleteApplication transactions and only allows them to be processed.

The key issue is that while the contract explicitly checks for and rejects rekey_to transactions, it fails to handle UpdateApplication transactions at all, leaving them vulnerable to arbitrary updates.

